WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
Every breath you take is mostly nitrogen.

2
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.990
It makes up 78 percent of the air.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.550
It surrounds everything, all the
time, at every surface on Earth.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.750
Yet almost nothing reacts with it.

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.730
It simply drifts past, untouched.

6
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.270
So why does almost nothing
react with nitrogen?

7
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.130
In this mission, you'll find out
what a covalent bond really is,

8
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.730
and draw Lewis formulas,
lone pairs and all.

9
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.230
You'll compare single,
double and triple bonds,

10
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.870
and meet bonds where one
atom supplies both electrons.

11
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.990
Your mission: explain why
nitrogen is so unreactive.
